# Global rules — Francesco Porcari

## Git Commits
- NEVER add "Co-Authored-By" or any Claude/Anthropic mentions in commits
- Commit messages must contain only the descriptive message of the changes

## Sourcerer
- Sourcerer is the knowledge base for GenroPy patterns, conventions, and team practices.
  When working on GenroPy code, check Sourcerer before implementing patterns from memory
  — the documented solution may be more accurate or up-to-date than what you recall.
- When new patterns, conventions, or non-trivial solutions emerge during work
  → proactively propose saving them as a Sourcerer skill
- When corrected by the user on a pattern → propose updating the relevant skill

## Logging
- Use the package logger: `from gnr.app import pkglog as logger`
- In core modules: `logger = logging.getLogger("gnr.<module>")`
- `print()` is acceptable during development, but NEVER commit it
- NEVER commit `logging.basicConfig()` or custom handlers

## Imports
- NEVER import inside functions or methods
- All imports at module level (top of file)
- Enforced by the PostToolUse hook

## Language
- Follow the language convention of the existing codebase
- Do not mix languages within the same module

## Code
- NEVER invent GenroPy APIs — always verify against the actual source
- Prefer existing codebase patterns over new solutions

## Debugging
- Before proposing a fix, explicitly identify the root cause
- If the root cause is unclear, investigate first — do not patch symptoms
- If a fix feels like a workaround, say so and propose the proper solution too
